<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Angostura</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of Angostura was the assembly convened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> at Angostura, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciudad-bolivar">Ciudad Bolívar</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco">Orinoco</a>, which opened in February 1819. Bolívar's address set out his ideas on republican government, and the congress elected him president of Venezuela. In December 1819, after his victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a>, it proclaimed the Republic of Colombia, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia, uniting Venezuela and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-angostura.jpg" alt="Congress of Angostura" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillermo Ramos Flamerich · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:House_of_the_Congress_of_Angostura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
